WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.460
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.150
Hi.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:06.990
I'm Carson.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.773
And I'm an Engineer of RStudio.

00:00:08.773 --> 00:00:10.440
And I'd like to show
you some work we've

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.770
been doing to make custom
theming easier inside of Shiny

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.907
and R Markdown.

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:17.740
I'd like to show you
two different packages.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.380
The first is bslib, which
allows you to essentially style

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.470
any of the components that are
rendered by your web browser

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.540
inside of an app or document.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.040
The second-- thematic allows
you to essentially translate

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.550
the CSS styles that you
include in your browser

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.940
and allow them to set new
defaults for your static R

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.320
plots.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.102
So to start using
bslib with shiny--

00:00:43.102 --> 00:00:45.060
the first thing that
you're going to want to do

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.040
is to call this bs_theme
function to create

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.370
a theming object,
which you can then

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.060
give to the theme argument
of essentially any page

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.500
layout inside of shiny that
wants to utilize Bootstrap.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.400
Now these currently by default,
what this is going to do

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.379
is actually upgrade
your application

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:08.790
from using Bootstrap 3
to using Bootstrap 4.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.490
So if you happen to put
this inside of an existing

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.910
application and you
encounter any issues,

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:18.450
just know that you can also
downgrade to Bootstrap 3

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.650
when using the bslib package.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.530
And in the future,
we plan on supporting

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.180
Bootstrap 5 and higher.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.210
And regardless of what
Bootstrap version you're using,

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.940
you can easily customize
the main colors and fonts

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.890
of your application.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.300
So here I've set the background
and foreground colors

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.750
to a dark mode
for my application

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.840
and the next I could choose
to set some important accent

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.840
colors like the primary
or secondary color.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.140
And finally, I will set
a different base font

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.060
from the Bootstrap defaults.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.690
So here I'm going to use the
font_google function, which

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:56.540
does a lot of work for me
in terms of making sure

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:59.810
that the font files are
available for the end user,

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.630
even if they don't have
an internet connection.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.510
And also keep in mind with
this bs_theme function,

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:09.050
you have access to hundreds of
different more specific styling

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.890
settings, if you want to get
more targeted with your styles

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.740
and to quickly preview
a given theme object,

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:19.070
try out this bs_theme_preview
function, which essentially

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.940
runs a demo app where you can
see all the various components

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.400
that your theme might impact.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.520
Now if you were to
include a bs_theme object

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.310
inside of your own
application, you

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.490
might notice that the
styling of your application

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.060
doesn't propagate to the static
R plots that are generated

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.980
by your Shiny app.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.750
And this is one of
the reasons why we

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.640
created the thematic package.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.790
If you call this thematic_shiny
function just prior

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:49.070
to running the
shiny application,

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:52.280
then all of the static R plots
that are generated by the Shiny

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:56.210
app will use the CSS
styles on their container

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:59.660
to set new theming
defaults on the R side.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.870
bslib also provides an
interactive theming tool,

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.990
which allows you to quickly
try out different theme settings

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.530
and seeing how that theme
renders in real-time.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.760
This theming tool can be used
with any Shiny application

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.470
by calling the
bs_themer function.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.830
The only requirement is that
you call the bs_themer function

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.300
inside of the server function.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.720
And that you're using
this interactive themer

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.410
with Bootstrap 4.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:31.410
Also keep in mind that if you're
running this themer locally,

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.690
any of the interactive
changes that you make

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.910
are captured with R code
and admitted to R console.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.300
So that you can copy
paste those changes

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.870
into your theme creation.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.950
Now if you'd like to use these
theming tools with R Markdown,

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.660
the first thing to
know is that you

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.570
can pass these theme
settings into the theme

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:51.030
parameter of an HTML document.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.580
In addition, if you'd like
to theme your document

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.800
with the interactive
theming tool,

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.070
you'll have to first add a
shiny runtime to your documents

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:02.640
YAML matter and then call
the bs_themer function

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.710
inside of the server side code.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.440
Now if you'd like these
real time changes in the CSS

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.210
on the page to influence the R
plots rendered by the document,

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.730
you'll first have
to enable thematic.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.670
And then also make sure that
your rendering your plots

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.529
through Shiny's renderPlot.

00:04:19.529 --> 00:04:22.320
It's also worth noting that
the matter can be used anywhere

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.040
to create any sort of
file format that you want.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.500
We've seen it used with Shiny
in our markdowns HTML document

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.670
to create PNG images, where
the styles are automatically

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.980
informed by CSS styles.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.060
However, you can also
enable thematic and give it

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.030
the actual color codes for
a background, foreground

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:47.750
and accent color, similar to
how we provided those things

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.820
to a bs_theme object.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:52.050
And finally, I would like
to thank you for listening.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.410
As well as provide these
links to the slides

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:58.020
as well as documentation,
where you can learn more.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.770
Thank you.

